---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What CS Offline is, how it works, and how it is licensed.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="About" title="About CS Offline" lead="Computer science with little or no technology, for grades 6–12." />
  <section class="on-paper band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="card prose" style="margin:0 auto">
        <h2>What it is</h2>
        <p>CS Offline is a free set of teacher and student resources for computer science, computational
          thinking, data science, AI literacy, cybersecurity, and ethics, taught without lots of
          technology. The activities, some of them games, use paper, cards, and conversation, and are
          organized into six learning domains. This website is where you find the activities, learn how
          they work, print what you need,
          and explore the ideas behind them.</p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>There are no accounts, cookies, or analytics, and the site loads nothing from other
          services. Nobody, student or teacher, gives any personal information to use it.</p>

        <h2 id="license">License</h2>
        <p>Licensing varies by activity. If an activity has an open license, such as Creative Commons,
          its page says so. Otherwise, all rights stay with its creator, so ask them before copying or
          adapting it.</p>

        <h2>Who makes it</h2>
        <p>CS Offline is designed by {SITE.author}, a computer science educator and designer. The
          project is developed in the open on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
